# Private checkout context — example only

Copy to AGENTS.local.md in the target checkout, exclude it from Git, and replace
these examples with real non-secret facts. The project's shared AGENTS.md must
explicitly instruct the agent to read this file; its name alone does not load it.

## Local environment

- This workstation has no GPU. Consult the configured private runbook for an
  already-authorized execution host when a task genuinely needs one.
- Use the existing project toolchain and lockfile. Record a local executable path
  here only if it differs from the portable project command.
- Local service instructions and checkout locations belong here when they differ
  from the team's standard setup. Verify the actual current state before acting.
- Keep account/model registries and machine access details in private configuration;
  point to the configured reference without copying credentials into instructions.

Shared checks and permissions still apply. These example preferences grant no
permission to deploy, spend money, change accounts, delete files or message others.
